  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The population of the Earth at the beginning of 1976 was four billion. Assume that the rate of growth is 2% per year.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write a formula for $P$, the population of the Earth in year $t$, $t\\geq1976$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=4\\times1.02^{t-1976}$ billion, $t\\geq1976$.",
          "worked": "The annual growth factor is $1+0.02=1.02$, and the elapsed time is $t-1976$ years.\n\n$$P=4\\times1.02^{t-1976}\\text{ billion},\\qquad t\\geq1976.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What will be the population in 2076? Give your answer in billions, correct to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$28.98$ billion.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P&=4\\times1.02^{2076-1976}\\\\P&=4\\times1.02^{100}\\\\P&\\approx28.98\\text{ billion}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "When will the population reach 10 billion?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "During 2022.\n\nSolve $1.02^{t-1976}=2.5$ using logarithms.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4\\times1.02^{t-1976}&=10\\\\1.02^{t-1976}&=2.5\\\\\\log_{10}\\!\\left(1.02^{t-1976}\\right)&=\\log_{10}2.5\\\\(t-1976)\\log_{10}1.02&=\\log_{10}2.5\\\\t-1976&=\\frac{\\log_{10}2.5}{\\log_{10}1.02}\\\\t&=1976+\\frac{\\log_{10}2.5}{\\log_{10}1.02}\\\\t&\\approx2022.27.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population reaches 10 billion during 2022.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
